Z||000036||firstfiero||12-10-2001||06:53 AM||||      I Don't know how long it will take you to figure this out blackstang but this is a fiero board. yay when someone calls their car a fiero eater were going to make fun of it.... go figure! I'm sure all the high class mustang fans on the other boards ...yea right.... would never have made any jokes if someone put a fiero up and called it a Mustang eater. Why are you here? When I had a bimmer I went to a bimmer board .The object of a message board is to find people that have the same interest in a car to hang out with. You like Mustangs.... nothing wrong with that...but why not go find a mustang board where everyone has the same love. <BR>      By the way people were making jokes about the web site. I didn't see one flame until you started to reply... as usual.<BR>       Sorry to flame ya dude but I just don't get why you hang out here. <P>------------------<BR><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000037||johnt671||12-10-2001||08:13 AM||||Magazine racing a joke.  Most magazines use the car makers numbers for performance because they lack the equipment to test the cars.||||reg||1
Z||000038||Oreif||12-10-2001||08:35 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackStang95:<BR><B>1990   Ford Mustang LX 5.0                     6.4           14.9<P>1990   Chevrolet Camaro Z28                   6.5            15.0<P>who'd be seeing tailpipes?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well, here in the REAL world, Nobody would see anyone's tailpipes. Why you may ask?<BR>At 0-60 feet. 1/10th of a second would be about 6" difference. At 1/4 mile would be about 1 foot of distance. If the Camaro sees the tailpipes of the Mustang, it's because the Mustang spun out at the end of the run!<P>For all REAL world purposes, the cars would be equal. I have yet to figure out why you even quoted a .1 second difference. Just have 2 different drivers for each car and you'll have 4 different times! Not even professional dragracers can go down the 1/4 mile and duplicate their times by .1 seconds.<P>Get a life.<BR>||||reg||1
