Z||000041||btoth||12-10-2001||10:06 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Smokin' GT:<BR><B>His car must not be too great then because that's not really much of a claim.  I mean, when a Fiero owner says "vette killer" or something, you have to be a little scared about what they've got under their hood.  While a 5.0 says "fiero killer" and we're like:<BR>     "Okay, so you've got a bunch more horsepower and a couple more cylinders... blow me!"<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I second that.  I actually like the car.  But <I>why</I> would you call it a "Fiero Killer"??  When most people think Fiero, they think 4-cyl or slow, or fire, or something similar  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">... so, wouldn't that just be insulting when you've got a 5 litre V8?  That'd be like labeling my GT as a "Geo killer".  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000042||BlackStang95||12-10-2001||01:17 PM||||Orief no ****  that a tenth of a second difference is an equal car, I posted it to shut up whoever said an old z28 would kill an old 5.0.  Everyone else could see that.<P>Whoever said the total bs times above, theyre incredibly off son, I guess thats why I dont read that magazine.  In Motortrend's recent test the 01 cobra ran 13.79 in the 1/4.  I've seen 14 flat runs on new gt's.  If you were wondering, the 02 camaro SS 35th beat the cobra by 2 tenths of a second, and costed over 3k more.  The article raved on how the Mustang was the better car.  <P>"The Mustang is a more balanced performer, a better daily driver, and as tested this time around, the better value.  Maybe thats why it gets to stick around."<P>Couldn't have said it better myself.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000043||Voytek||12-10-2001||02:24 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by btoth:<BR><B> I second that.  I actually like the car.  But <I>why</I> would you call it a "Fiero Killer"??  When most people think Fiero, they think 4-cyl or slow, or fire, or something similar   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">... so, wouldn't that just be insulting when you've got a 5 litre V8?  That'd be like labeling my GT as a "Geo killer".   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Good analogy, btoth.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>BS95 - The owner of that Stang obviously thinks higher of Fieros than you do.  Comparing his Cobra to a Fiero says a lot.<P>Remember what I said about 'another chance' in your 'Should I leave?' thread?  Well, here it is, staring you in the face.  Think about it.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000044||LoW_KeY||12-10-2001||03:21 PM||||Well we all know the fatter wallet gets you the faster car.. <P>hell I'll go up against any stock stang, done it before do it again..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I mean there both nice cars yes, but I just hate when the fiero gets bashed for being a slow ugly car.<P>I get looks from everyone even guys drivin new vettes, I mean its seems only older people/mature people know the true values of cars its not about the speed but what you like.<P>Besides any idiot can race in a straight line.. taking corners at a high rate of speed requires skill and in a straight line of course the bigger engine might win, but if that was the case I'd be proving a lot of people wrong then...<P>My brother had an awesome 88 LX stang 5.0 *cough* 4.8 liter that had 250 hp.<P>He rode in my fiero and almost had a mess in the seat and even told me it'd be one hell of a race vs his car.  Even let him drive it and he knows.. he's owned many stangs.<P>heck I'm really opened minded on a bunch of cars.. but are the owners to me? no because I drive a fiero and it catches fire all that good stuff.<P>Why can't everyone just look past the speed part, everyone drives their car for some reason it makes each of us unique, I mean wouldn't it be pretty boring driving the same car as everyone else? were gettin there.. they're all pretty much bubble lookin' now days  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>AIM: FierFormula88   <P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/low_keysig.gif"> ||||reg||1
