Z||000047||GTFiero1||12-10-2001||05:04 PM||||remember Car and Diver from about a year ago "CAMARO Vs. MUSTANG" the camaro whooped the musangs @$$ i saw the TV special and i have that mag some where. just to state, my step brother who just got out of the military use to on a mustang but now owns a GTO. When i asked his why did he by the ford mustang his reply was " i was young and stupid at the time and just went for looks" i am not lying either. oh,oh any stock mustang 5.0 can beat a stock fiero- hmmm comparing a 2.8V-6 to a 5.0 V-8 gee... no put an equal size engine in the fiero and that mustang is gonna show up in the fieros rear view mirror. i know you probably think im just some little sh*t but i know a LOT about cars.. a LOT. <P>------------------<BR>Adam J. B.<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fiero_3.jpg">   <BR>you gotta keep on keepin on...<BR>IM AOL: GTFiero &  Rumpdetective (dont ask)||||reg||1
Z||000048||Groove Champion||12-10-2001||05:16 PM||||It seems as though the only time I post is when the word "Mustang" is mentioned.<P>Someone mentioned a quote from a magazine saying how well a balanced performer the mustang is. I have seen this and it was spoken in reference to a Cobra , NOT your run of the mill 5.0ltr. Lets not even compare a Cobra R to a regular 5.0ltr or a Cobra , I have driven them back to back , completley different animal.<P>A fiero with an engine swap is a far better platform for performance than a 5.0ltr mustang in quite a few respects. But what is the defined purpose? If were talking stop light grandprixs I will take the Fiero , Lighter , better rear suspension , engine over the Drive wheels , a Killer in every respect. It's all about the first 60 feet on the street.<P>If your talking Trailered it to the track to Drag race , sub 10 sec car, Give me the mustang for the simple reason that there is a greater aftermarket source for drag racers. <P>As for the IROC vs. 5.0ltr debate , On a long Straight a 1LE IROC would pull away in showroom stock class over a 5.0ltr. Anyone can debate this to death if you would like , but keep in mind I have spent the last 30 or so years racing mustangs , I know what an IROCs taillights look like. Were not talking a little street race , were talking watkins glen , road atlanta , mosport , you name it. The lighter weight of an LX made it more durable whan it came to making tires and brakes last. Also a bit more nimble through the Esses. <P>It all comes down to torque , the TPi L98 in the IRoc was a killer off the corners and more than made up for the weight. Ask anyone who has an L98 in a Vette or a Fiero. Greater low end than an LT1 , but runs out of breath fairly quickly.<P>You Guys argue on the basis of Magazines. Magazines sell cars , thats it. If you put all your faith in what a publication has to say your a very misguided individual. I can remember a press date when I worked with ford. We had a Grand National and a LX 5.0ltr with no air , 5spd , trunk. The 5.0ltr was a stripper , At the end of the day the 5.0ltr was faster, by only a couple 100ths of a second , but the 5.0ltr was quicker.<P>Now I can hear the grand National owners crying fowl....<P>I think Oreif said it best..... Get a life. I won't name names , but some of you who argue magazines all day long have never been in a fast car in your life. You put all your faith in the glossy pages of automotive propaganda.<P>I do have to say though , as someone who recieves actual industry tests On everything going , someone here very favourably curves their times to try and prove a point. GTMike caught you on that one<P>If you would like to argue any of my points I have brought up keep a few things in mind<P>I'm on my 23rd Mustang  all but 2 of them have been V8's , the others were SVO's<BR>I have raced mustangs since the early 70's<BR>I was running the back straight at Mosport @ over 130mph in a 5.0ltr when most of you were learning to parallel park your moms minivan.<P>Ok...now I'm done and I will get off the podium.<P>GC.<BR>87 GT ..all torn to hell right now..in search of a small block. ||||reg||1
