Z||000056||Fformula88||12-11-2001||10:21 AM||||These magazine numbers can be very deceptive.  Unless the numbers from both cars came from the same test, don't even bother posting if they are close (say .5 sec either way 0-60).  The same car, tested different days will have different times based on tons of factors, weather, barometric pressure, altitude, driver skill, the cars own engine (each is slightly different) and on and on.<P>So if BS's numbers are from the SAME test, then the 'Stang did win.  But those numbers are so close that I wouldn't go bragging too much.<P>If the numbers are close, from different tests, or worse different magazines then don't even bother posting them.  The only thing they tell us is the cars would be competitive with each other.<P>Example:  Motor Trend has tested different Celica GT-S's which ran 0-60 times between 6.6 sec and 7.3 sec.  Thats a .7 difference to 60 for the same car, with the same engine.||||reg||1
Z||000057||banditbalz||12-11-2001||10:32 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Galen:<BR><B>I just thought that guy naming his car Fiero eater was funny, you ppl have a real security issue ya know   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> hehe<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>funy part is, I raced that same year, same model Mustang with a 5 speed and minor mods. He lost bad in the quarter mile. Several passes and the best the Mustang could muster was a 15.2 Yeah he had lot's of excuses like traction problems and his car was heavier.<BR>There were 2 5.0L mustangs running the same times that day.<BR>Anyways, calling a 5.0L Mustang a FieroEater is a little far fetched. You need a little  more than 225 hp to run with me...<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!||||reg||1
Z||000058||Groove Champion||12-11-2001||11:51 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackStang95:<BR><B>*yawn*<P>im about done with this thread.<P>I wanted to say though, you sound just like ricers when you whine about the displacement difference between the 2.8 and 4.8 (5.0).  You guys sit here and talk so much ****  about mustangs but when someone points out the clear fact they are faster you're like well yeah, but if we do swaps and blah blah blah.  That's straight ricer crap.  You can make any, and i mean any car fast with swaps.  That goes without saying.  <P>I really don't understand why you guys talk down mustangs so much.  That'd be like the Mustang guys talking ****  about how they can beat vipers and ferraris.  You don't see that happen, because they aren't ignorant and fanatical about their rides.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I think that you have made it quite clear through your posts that your the ignorant one.<P>And for gods sake , Please don't compare a mustang to a ferrari. Good lord Boy , you really need to ride in a car other than a mustang , then perhaps you will see that their are quite a few faults with them. I love mustangs to death , but I also have a perspective of what other marks can do. As for engine swaps in a fiero , Dollar for Dollar you really can't beat it. <P>If anything I feel sorry for you blackstang , day after day sticking up for Mustangs , did you notice that the real Hardcore mustang guys don't bother? I believe there was even a member here with a V8 fiero and a couple 5.0ltrs. You didn't see him talking out his a** , He knew what his car was , and what it wasn't. <P>Just my 2 cents..<P>GC<P><BR>||||reg||1
