Z||000070||Groove Champion||12-11-2001||08:12 PM||||Blackstang , your level of intelligence just keeps coming through.<P>Slammed Fiero's post was very funny indeed  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I had heard around from some forum members that banditBalz's car ran low 15's , Very impressive. His times are faster than I can muster in my 5spd GT 5.0. But I guess I don't have the experience a harcore racer like yourself has (Blackstang) I have only been racing mustangs for 2 decades ...how long had you been running them again?<P>Why do I buy Mustang after mustang.<P>Lets see.. ..Oh yes... I WORKED FOR FORD FOR 26 YEARS!! I got great deals , they were a cheap car to race and there was lots of competition in the classes that I ran. I got some factory and dealership backing when available (late 70's was rough due to the economy)<P>The thing I have to wonder about , is why bother with a 6cyl mustang? and why bother with the Fiero forum at all? do you post on Mustang forums at all?? I have never seen a person with 6cyl mustangs act the way you do, usually the types of conversations you instigate can be heard in the parking lots of Highschools across the country..Where some kid beat a new z28 with his 6cyl Mustang...but unfortunatley no one was there to see it... You brag about your K&N filters and think they actually add 17hp , mention Rear wheels Horsepower and you scratch your head and wonder where else the HP could be.<P>If there's one thing that annoys me it's ignorance. there seems to be no lack of it coming from blackstang. He more than likley got laughfed off the mustang forums , so he came here. I have to wonder if he is compensating for some other short comings?<P><BR>blackstang , I have had 23 mustangs , and even the slowest ones were faster than your 6cyl lumberwagon could ever hope to be.<P>GC.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000071||Slammed Fiero||12-11-2001||08:20 PM||||Blackstang just got BURNED!!!<P>How can you argue experience? You can't.<P>As for banditbalzs car. I believe he has video , and numerous witneses to his run.<P>His wife <BR>grinthock<BR>Jay (northstar fiero)<BR>Lots of GTA Fieroclub members.<P>But your probably right seems a little fishy , he probably paid them to say that and had the video made to make dorks with 6cyl mustangs look bad..Oh wait...6cyl mustang ...mission accomplished.<P>Banditbalzs you Crafty Devil you!!<P>Jonathan M.<BR> <P><p>[This message has been edited by Slammed Fiero (edited 12-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000072||Oreif||12-11-2001||08:53 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Spektrum-87GT:<BR><B>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"> a completely stock fastback fiero gt running low 15s... i'd like to see that... can anyone back that up? its not hard for me to believe a slightly modified fastback gt can run low 15's its the fact that he says its completely stock, if i remember correctly, didnt professional drivers only turn low 16's? thats a heck of a difference for a completely stock non professional driver... <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Road and Track <BR>July 1985<P>Red 85 Fiero GT<BR>1/4 mile times out of 4 runs<BR>Slowest 15.6<BR>Fastest 15.2<P>This was stock right from Pontiac with a V-6 and a 4-spd. The article said with racing tires it would be better. They had some traction problems off the line.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000073||My7Fieros||12-11-2001||08:55 PM||||(Sigh) BS95, Im still scratching my head trying to figure out what your deal is. Why do you come here and do nothing but smart off and bash Fieros?<BR>I own a Mustang also, 2001. Its a nice car, but my Fieros are my "true love". If I feel the need to talk about Mustangs, I go to the Mustang forum..although I rarely do (maybe 9 or 10 post since I bought the Mustang in March). I even made mention of my Fieros and everybody there was like "yeah Fieros are cool, Ive got a friend who has one and blah blah blah"....hell, even "StungByMyStang" who is on the Mustang forum joined Pennocks, and has had nothing but GOOD things to say about Fieros. If people here bother you, just go over to the Stang forum where you're among your "own kind"...k? jeez......<BR>(BTW my Fieros w/ run circles around my Mustang  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> )||||reg||1
Z||000074||LoW_KeY||12-11-2001||09:18 PM||||How bout a closed thread?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I agree with everyone else, it'd be like me being on a stang board and talking stuff about a fiero.. find a stang board man, many of us know what our cars are capable of and don't need someone who owns a stang to tell us what their capable of.<P>The fiero was under rated from the factory.. you know its called misconception many cars back during the 60's, early 70's did that.  My dad told me about a car that was rated 300 hp? which actually had 375.. not all fieros have 140.. sure as hell tell ya my old 2.8 didn't, but I won't even go into detail.. can anyone direct this misguided person to the stang board? links please  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000075||BlackStang95||12-11-2001||09:37 PM||||HaHa, it's amazing how everyone jumps on the bandwagon and says the same thing everyone else says.  I'll respond to everyone individually though.<P>bandit: "Glad you figured it out... Look buddy, you bought a Mustang with a 3.8, Sorry about your luck! You wanna play? Bring the wagen up here to St. Thomas or Toronto Motorsport Park and we'll see what a Mustang can do. Till then, you're just talking out your ass."<P><BR>I'm not the one talking **** , saying I can beat cars that are way better than me, etc, you are, so you can bring your candyass down to va if you wanna prove something to me.<P>Orief...15.2 out of road and track...not bad<BR>bandits claiming he got well faster than that<BR>Too bad the 5.0's all ran mid-high 14's.  Even the guy with the 5.0 that couldn't drive from banditz story hit 15.2.<P>I've never bashed fieros once, I'm just not gonna sit and agree they can beat something they can't, no matter what the hell it is.  <P>The fiero has more than 140?  anyone dynoed this?  didn't think so....talking outta your ass again.<P>Groove you seem like the typical "im old and i know everything" guy.  I've never driven a 5.0 stang, but hanging out at the track I've never seen one run above 15.  Sounds like you just can't drive.  Sorry.<P>Why a v-6 mustang?  I love the styling, it performs fine, and it was cheap.  I actually like cars built within the last decade or so.  <P>I post a lot at v-6 mustang message boards.  The community is huge, definitely bigger than the fiero one.  Plenty of guys running 12's and 13's on a 3.8.  14's are easy to break into, I'm gonna be doing that next summer sometime.     <P>Who's next??||||reg||1
