Z||000079||stingant0||12-11-2001||10:35 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackStang95:<BR><B>Orief no ****  that a tenth of a second difference is an equal car, I posted it to shut up whoever said an old z28 would kill an old 5.0.  Everyone else could see that.<P>Whoever said the total bs times above, theyre incredibly off son, I guess thats why I dont read that magazine.  In Motortrend's recent test the 01 cobra ran 13.79 in the 1/4.  I've seen 14 flat runs on new gt's.  If you were wondering, the 02 camaro SS 35th beat the cobra by 2 tenths of a second, and costed over 3k more.  The article raved on how the Mustang was the better car.  <P>"The Mustang is a more balanced performer, a better daily driver, and as tested this time around, the better value.  Maybe thats why it gets to stick around."<P>Couldn't have said it better myself.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well I have to differ, I have seen a WS6 T/A run 13.2 in the 1/4 mile (even have it on tape) it was an automatic with a removed air filter. I have 01 Cobras on tape, the best they ran was 16.5 yes 16.5 most of the time they were runing 17s. But they didn't know how to drive it. My point is that the car doesn't drive you (unless you have an automatic) but you drive the car. ||||reg||1
