Z||000083||Pyric||12-11-2001||11:49 PM||||Well this is going nowhere fast.  Comparing cars like this never does.  There are too many factors that contribute to how fast a car can make a run.  Driver, engine, weight, handling etc.  <P>BlackStang95, we're all happy that you like Mustangs and I bet your Mamma is proud... but you are in the wrong place to be starting this argument AGAIN.<P>Why not check the archives, I know it is in about 12 of those threads in the past month.<P>FACT #1:  Being that this is a Fiero forum... You will NOT win.  <P>FACT #2: Almost everyone here has either:<BR>A) Wasted a Mustang (in a Fiero or not)<BR>B) Been in the car with someone while they did.<P>or<P>C) Watched a car that "statistically" should not have stood a chance, burn one.<P>The whole POINT behind this post in the first place was that saying the mustang was a "Fiero Killer"  was like me calling my Nissan a BMX killer.  It isn't something that should be so astounding that you name your vehicle for it.<P>Now, I have a great respect for any car with potential. (including Mustangs).  But I don't start a flame war when I see a car I like get ragged on.  Get over it, because you wont win.  <P><BR><P>------------------<BR>  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieronegS.jpg">  <P>"Never offend people with style when you can offend them with substance." <BR>--Sam Brown||||reg||1
