Z||000085||Oreif||12-12-2001||12:13 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackStang95:<BR><B><P>Too bad the 5.0's all ran mid-high 14's.  <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That is incorrect. Many of the mid 80's 5.0's were mid/high 15's. The "who's faster" between the Ford Mustang and the GM F-bodies started in the early 80's. Most Mustangs and F-bodies were in the 15's. Even the Corvette had a year or two when they were running 15's in the 1/4! Not until the late 80's when Ford up'd the HP and GM dropped in the 350's in place of the 305's did the 1/4 mile times get into the 14's.<P><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 12-12-2001).]||||reg||1
